        "block_id": "87c444fd-baf1-4da3-ae22-4c2f81d49298",
        "start_offset": 328,
        "end_offset": 2328,
        "quote_text": "## Severity\r\n\r\n- **Severity:** Low\r\n- **CVSS v3.1:** `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N` (3.7, Low)\r\n- **CWE:** CWE-440 (Expected Behavior Violation), CWE-668 (Exposure of Resource to Wrong Sphere)\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nvLLM V1 `InputBatch.condense()` can leave a stale `allowed_token_ids_mask_cpu_tensor` row after moving a constrained request. A later unrestricted request that reuses that batch slot inherits the previous request's token allowlist, so sampling for that other client is constrained by a mask it did not set (cross-request output-integrity issue). The victim request still returns HTTP 200 with no error indication.\r\n\r\nPublic report: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/43894\r\n\r\n## Affected\r\n\r\n- **Ecosystem / package:** pip / `vllm`\r\n- **Affected versions:** vLLM ≤ 0.30.0 (V1 worker `InputBatch` path). Confirmed via public issue #43894.\r\n- **Fixed versions:** Fix merged in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/43931 (not yet in a tagged release as of v0.30.0; expected in the next release).\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n`InputBatch.condense()` copies `allowed_token_ids_mask_cpu_tensor` from a moved request's row into the freed index but never clears the source row. `add_request()` only writes that row when the new request sets `sampling_params.allowed_token_ids`. When another active request still has `allowed_token_ids`, `_make_sampling_metadata()` copies the active prefix of the CPU mask to GPU and `Sampler.apply_logits_processors()` applies the stale whitelist to the unrestricted request.\r\n\r\nAn attacker who can submit generate traffic (including unauthenticated `/invocations`, which is outside `--api-key` guards, or any valid API key on `/v1`) plants a chosen `allowed_token_ids` mask. If batching/`condense` recycles that row onto another client's unrestricted request while the constrained request is still active, the victim's tokens are limited to the attacker's allowlist (for example only a single token, only digit tokens, or only tokens that spell a",
